※ Thirty-two values are wanted at once, which is more registers than any of
※ the three architectures has: fourteen on one, twenty-eight and twenty-six
※ on the others.  What does not fit goes to the frame and is read back.
※
※ They are written back in the reverse of the order they were read, so the
※ first is wanted across every other one; returning it is what says it came
※ back from the frame unchanged.

